### Task Management API - Local Testing
### Base URL: http://localhost:3001/api/v1
###
### This file uses REST Client extension for VS Code
### Install: https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=humao.rest-client
###
### Or use with IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client
###
### HOW TO USE:
### 1. First, run the "Register New User" request to create an account
### 2. Then, run the "Login User" request (marked with @name login)
### 3. All subsequent requests will AUTOMATICALLY use the tokens from the login response
### 4. No need to manually copy/paste tokens!
###
### The automatic token extraction uses this syntax:
### {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}} - Gets access token from login response
### {{login.response.body.data.tokens.refreshToken}} - Gets refresh token from login response

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api/v1

###############################################
# Health Check
###############################################

### Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health HTTP/1.1

###############################################
# Authentication
###############################################

### 1. Register New User
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!@#",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}

### 2. Register Another User (for testing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!@#",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith"
}

### 3. Login User
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!@#"
}

###

### 4. Get User Profile (Protected Route)
# Automatically uses token from login response above
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}

### 5. Refresh Access Token
# Automatically uses refresh token from login response above
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.data.tokens.refreshToken}}"
}

### 6. Logout
# Automatically uses token from login response above
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.data.tokens.accessToken}}

###############################################
# Error Testing
###############################################

### Test - Register with Weak Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "weak",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User"
}

### Test - Register with Duplicate Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!@#",
  "firstName": "Duplicate",
  "lastName": "User"
}

### Test - Login with Wrong Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!@#"
}

### Test - Login with Non-existent Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!@#"
}

### Test - Access Protected Route Without Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile HTTP/1.1

### Test - Access Protected Route With Invalid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer invalid_token_here

### Test - Refresh with Invalid Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "invalid_refresh_token"
}

###############################################
# Manual Token Testing
# (Replace with actual tokens from login response)
###############################################

### Manual - Get Profile with Custom Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Manual - Refresh with Custom Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

